# Keycloak

Keycloak is the central identity provider.

Use standard protocols:

- OAuth 2.0
- OpenID Connect

Prefer standard Keycloak configuration over custom code.

Realm configuration should be reproducible.

Clients must have:

- explicit redirect URIs
- explicit web origins
- appropriate client authentication settings
- least-privilege access

Never use wildcard redirect URIs in production.

Do not put sensitive business data into tokens unnecessarily.

Roles should remain coarse-grained.

Resource-level authorization belongs in the application unless
there is a strong reason to move it into the identity layer.